    {
      "id": "claim_90b5b1f0db894b4eb33525cc8501dff3",
      "statement": "Database operations are not wrapped in managed transaction or error-handling behavior: connect happens immediately in the constructor, execute_query commits each execution, and callers must explicitly close the stored cursor and connection; failures in these operations are not caught by the helper.",
